    "text": {
     "en": "Maharashtra has 444 tigers. Madhya Pradesh has 341 more tigers than Maharashtra.\n444 + 341 = 785. Madhya Pradesh has 785 tigers.\nUttarakhand has 116 more than Maharashtra: 444 + 116 = 560 tigers.\nTotal across the three states: 444 + 785 + 560 = 1789 tigers.\nUse tokens or box diagrams to solve until you can do it without them.\nMultiplying in hundreds: 3 × 200 = 600."
